[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/comments/63735369","html_url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/5659#issuecomment-63735369","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/5659","id":63735369,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYzNzM1MzY5","user":{"login":"WestLangley","id":1000017,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDAwMTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1000017?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley","html_url":"https://github.com/WestLangley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2014-11-19T23:34:36Z","updated_at":"2014-11-19T23:48:20Z","body":"Welcome back, @bhouston : - )\n\nThis appears to be a numerical issue. And, unfortunately, if it happens with \"ZYX\", it will be easy to construct equivalent cases with other Euler orders.\n\nIn `Euler.setFromQuaternion()`, up to rounding error, we end up making this call\n\n```\nMath.atan2( 0, 0 );\n```\n\nIt is easy to construct problem quaternions:\n\n```\nvar a = Math.random();\nvar b = Math.random();\nvar q1 = new THREE.Quaternion( a, -b,  a, b ).normalize(); // pattern 1\nvar q2 = new THREE.Quaternion( a,  b, -a, b ).normalize(); // pattern 2\n```\n\nThese are interesting quaternions. They represent a rotation that, in words, can be expressed as:\n\n> rotate by some angle around the z-axis, and then rotate a quarter-turn around the y-axis.\n\nThis is a Gimbal-lock situation. What is the use case that lead to these operations?\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/comments/63735369/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"WestLangley","id":1000017,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDAwMTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1000017?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley","html_url":"https://github.com/WestLangley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WestLangley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":195862060,"node_id":"MDE0Ok1lbnRpb25lZEV2ZW50MTk1ODYyMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/events/195862060","actor":{"login":"bhouston","id":588541,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4ODU0MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/588541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhouston","html_url":"https://github.com/bhouston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhouston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhouston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"h